le group, forms amide then carboxylic acid, liberating ammonia.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Experimentally demonstrated, robust pathway for glycine in surface pools; see Patel et al. (2015, Nature Chemistry).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_002\",\n      \"name\": \"Glyoxylate reductive amination (iron-catalyzed) to glycine\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_006\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_001\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"Elemental iron\", \"Ferrous iron\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"343K (70\u00b0C)\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Fe^0, Fe^2+\",\n        \"aqueous\": \"true\",\n        \"other\": \"Mildly alkaline\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Reductive amination of the \u03b1-keto acid by hydroxylamine with iron metals providing reducing equivalents.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Direct experimental support for iron-driven glycine synthesis; see Muchowska et al. (2019, Nature).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_003\",\n      \"name\": \"Peracetic acid amination to glycine\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_001\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"370-420K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": \"true\",\n        \"other\": \"Hydrothermal vent, oxidizing conditions\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Ammonia attacks carbonyl carbon of peracetic acid, displacing peroxide, yielding glycine.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Reported as robust glycine synthesis pathway under hydrothermal vent simulation; see Aubrey et al. (2008, Origins Life Evol. Biosph.).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_004\",\n      \"name\": \"L-Serine thermal decomposition\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_009\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_001\", \"mol_010\"],\n      \"environment\": \