tate with water-derived species, forms glycolic acid.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"UV-driven route validated by Liu et al. (2021, Nature Chem).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pathways\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyanosulfidic surface aminonitrile hydrolysis\",\n      \"description\": \"Aminoacetonitrile forms under HCN-rich surface pools, then hydrolyzes to glycine during aqueous wet phases.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_002\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"name\": \"Iron-catalyzed hydrothermal reductive amination of glyoxylate\",\n      \"description\": \"Hydrothermal glyoxylate reacts with hydroxylamine in the presence of iron to furnish glycine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_002\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_006\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrothermal peracetic acid amination\",\n      \"description\": \"Peracetic acid generated from acetate oxidizes, then reacts with ammonia to make glycine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_003\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"name\": \"Serine retro-aldol decomposition\",\n      \"description\": \"L-Serine undergoes retro-aldol cleavage in hot hydrothermal waters, yielding glycine and formaldehyde.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_004\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_009\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"name\": \"L-Threonine direct thermal decomposition to glycine\",\n      \"description\": \"Hot hydrothermal conditions decarboxylate threonine directly to glycine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_005\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_011\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"name\": \"L-Threonine decomposition to glycine and ethylene oxide\",\n      \"description\": \"Alternative threonine breakdown route; f